\f0\fs24 \cf0 The height profile file looks like this (see also attached file example):\
\
The first line consists of four comma-separated numbers: #x, #z, dx, dz\
#x: number of grid points in x-direction, \
#z: number of grid points in z-direction, \
dx: distance of points in x-direction (unit mm), \
dz: distance of points in z-direction (unit mm).\
\
The heights (unit: nm) at the net points follow in the next lines, always first along the z-direction.\
height[1,1]\
height[1,2]\
\'85\
height[1,#z]\
height[2,1]\
height[2,2]\
\'85\
height[#x,#z-1]\
height[#x,#z]\
\
The grid is always set symmetrically around the centre (z=0, x=0) of the mirror. \
\
If only one line profile along the z-direction is available, one has to double it to two x-positions, e.g. the edges of the mirror.\
}